<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="defs_P_9_6" targetNamespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <process id="P_9_6" name="9.6 Manage wildfire operational response" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>9.6.2, 9.6.3 and 9.6.4 are drawn. The plan and the deenergization criteria at 9.6.1 are a standing record AND a determination the pack supplies no rules for, so they are specified twice over.

This path deliberately begins after an authorised shutoff decision exists. The Source Authority Pack names no wildfire deenergization or public-safety shutoff authority at all - no criteria, no approval route, no notice timing, no notice content, no cancellation rule - and 16 U.S.C. 824o(a)(1) excludes local distribution from the federal bulk-power definition, so it supplies none either. Drawing the decision gate would mean inventing the thresholds on which a utility de-energises a community. What is drawn is what happens once somebody with the authority has decided: execute, notify, patrol, restore, and assemble the evidence.</documentation>
    <laneSet id="P_9_6_lanes">
      <lane id="l_96_no" name="Network operations">
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_start</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_scope</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_exec</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_rec</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_mon</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_dir</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_wait</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_area</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_rest</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
      <lane id="l_96_cs" name="Customer and public safety">
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_note</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
      <lane id="l_96_frd" name="Patrol">
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_pat</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_dg</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_rep</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
      <lane id="l_96_mai" name="Evidence and cost">
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_ev</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_link</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_gap2</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_pkg</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_96_end</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>
    <startEvent id="n_96_start" name="Authorised shutoff decision exists"><conditionalEventDefinition id="n_96_start_cd"><condition/></conditionalEventDefinition></startEvent>
    <userTask id="n_96_scope" name="Confirm the authorised deenergization scope and timing"><documentation>9.6.2. The criteria and the authority are the operator's; this step confirms what was decided, it does not decide.</documentation></userTask>
    <userTask id="n_96_exec" name="Execute deenergization and record affected assets"><documentation>9.6.2.</documentation></userTask>
    <sendTask id="n_96_note" name="Issue customer and public-safety notices"><documentation>9.6.2. The pack states no notice timing or content, so neither is drawn. Recording what was sent and when is still owed.</documentation></sendTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_96_rec" name="Record affected locations, event time, notice status"><documentation>9.6.2.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <receiveTask id="n_96_mon" name="Monitor conditions and publish status changes"><documentation>9.6.2.</documentation></receiveTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_96_dir" name="Patrol authorised"/>
    <userTask id="n_96_wait" name="Hold deenergized"><documentation>9.6.3. Patrol begins on direction, not on the weather improving.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_96_area" name="Assign patrol areas with access and hazard information"><documentation>9.6.3.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <userTask id="n_96_pat" name="Inspect and record damage, no-damage or inaccessible"><documentation>9.6.3. Inaccessible is a third outcome and not a silent no-damage. 29 CFR 1910.269(m) governs the deenergized condition the patrol works under.</documentation></userTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_96_dg" name="Section clear"/>
    <sendTask id="n_96_rep" name="Create repair work and hold the section"><documentation>9.6.3. A damaged section stays held; it does not re-energise because the rest of the circuit is ready.</documentation></sendTask>
    <userTask id="n_96_rest" name="Restore released sections and update customers"><documentation>9.6.3.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_96_ev" name="Collect shutoff, notice, patrol, restoration and cost records"><documentation>9.6.4.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <userTask id="n_96_link" name="Validate event, time, asset, location and work links"><documentation>9.6.4. Documentation is carried on MAI: IEC 61968-6 cl. 4.2 has no document-management component and the gap is recorded rather than filled with an invented code.</documentation></userTask>
    <userTask id="n_96_gap2" name="Identify missing, conflicting and unsupported evidence"><documentation>9.6.4.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_96_pkg" name="Assemble the evidence and cost package"><documentation>9.6.4. The pack states no jurisdictional filing content, retention period or recovery rule, so the package is assembled to the operator's own specification.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <endEvent id="n_96_end" name="Event evidence packaged"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_start_n_96_scope" sourceRef="n_96_start" targetRef="n_96_scope" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_scope_n_96_exec" sourceRef="n_96_scope" targetRef="n_96_exec" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_exec_n_96_note" sourceRef="n_96_exec" targetRef="n_96_note" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_note_n_96_rec" sourceRef="n_96_note" targetRef="n_96_rec" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_rec_n_96_mon" sourceRef="n_96_rec" targetRef="n_96_mon" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_mon_n_96_dir" sourceRef="n_96_mon" targetRef="n_96_dir" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_dir_n_96_wait" sourceRef="n_96_dir" targetRef="n_96_wait" name="not yet"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[patrolAuthorised = false]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_wait_n_96_mon" sourceRef="n_96_wait" targetRef="n_96_mon" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_dir_n_96_area" sourceRef="n_96_dir" targetRef="n_96_area" name="authorised"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_area_n_96_pat" sourceRef="n_96_area" targetRef="n_96_pat" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_pat_n_96_dg" sourceRef="n_96_pat" targetRef="n_96_dg" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_dg_n_96_rep" sourceRef="n_96_dg" targetRef="n_96_rep" name="damage or inaccessible"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[sectionClear = false]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_rep_n_96_ev" sourceRef="n_96_rep" targetRef="n_96_ev" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_dg_n_96_rest" sourceRef="n_96_dg" targetRef="n_96_rest" name="clear"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_rest_n_96_ev" sourceRef="n_96_rest" targetRef="n_96_ev" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_ev_n_96_link" sourceRef="n_96_ev" targetRef="n_96_link" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_link_n_96_gap2" sourceRef="n_96_link" targetRef="n_96_gap2" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_gap2_n_96_pkg" sourceRef="n_96_gap2" targetRef="n_96_pkg" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_96_pkg_n_96_end" sourceRef="n_96_pkg" targetRef="n_96_end" name=""/>
  </process>
